    {
      "type": "Environmental",
      "requirement": "If a marine mammal is observed entering or within the relevant Level B harassment zone prior to beginning a specified activity, the activity must be delayed. If the activity is ongoing, it must be shut down immediately, unless shutdown would result in imminent risk of injury or loss of life to an individual, pile refusal, or pile instability. The activity must not commence or resume until the animal(s) has been confirmed to have left and is on a path away from the Level B harassment zone or after 15 minutes for small odontocetes and pinnipeds, and 30 minutes for all other species with no further sightings.",
      "scope": "Within the Level B harassment zone",
      "source": "50 CFR 217.264(a)",
      "related_domains": ["Environmental", "Safety"]
    },
    {
      "type": "Safety",
      "requirement": "For in-water construction heavy machinery activities, if a marine mammal is on a path towards or comes within 10 meters (m) (32.8 feet) of equipment, LOA Holder must cease operations until the marine mammal has moved more than 10 m on a path away from the activity to avoid direct interaction with equipment.",
      "scope": "Within 10 meters of in-water construction equipment",
      "source": "50 CFR 217.264(a)(9)",
      "related_domains": ["Safety"]
    },
    {
      "type": "Technical",
      "requirement": "All vessels must be equipped with a properly installed, operational Automatic Identification System (AIS) device and LOA Holder must report all Maritime Mobile Service Identify (MMSI) numbers to NMFS Office of Protected Resources.",
